 "diagnosis": {
  "verdict": "More (and more balanced) data lowered variance and lifted recall.",
  "reasoning": "The set grew to 523 images with unsafe nearly doubled (272 safe / 251 unsafe, 1.08:1), so the classes are now close to balanced. Best test ROC-AUC rose to 0.979 (past the old ~0.93 plateau) and the recall-priority operating point reaches 95% unsafe-recall at 86% accuracy. The overfit gap shrank for most backbones (e.g. ResNet50 test error roughly halved) and per-model AUC improved across the board, so the model is less variance-limited than before. Remaining errors are a few tiny/occluded hangers and genuinely ambiguous doorway poses."
 }
